ave the  same brainwaves but simon williams never  told wanda this it's unclear if he was  even aware of it at the time but once  when wanda and vision actually get  together wonder man realizes that he has  feelings for wanda and is pretty bummed  out about it now there's a lot to the  story but basically for the point of  this wonder man series and the scarlet  witch returning in the mcu what happens  is is we get white vision and he loses  all of his emotions so wanda goes to  wonder man and asks him if he could lend  his brain waves again to give vision his  emotions again in which he actually says  no because he has feelings for wanda and  doesn't want her to be with vision  however eventually he does cave and he  says okay but white vision does not want  them he says i have to go out and i have  to discover my emotions for myself and  get my own personality not your  personality so he leaves and eventually  when he leaves wonder man and wanda get  together and it's also very important to  know that in the comics wonder man dies  but wanda actually resurrects him in his  ionic form this is pretty much exactly  what we saw in one division one to  resurrected vision in kind of an ionic  form as well because obviously the  vision wasn't permanent and could not  live outside of the bubble that wanna  created just like her kids however we  did have white vision or spectral vision  as some people call him he appeared at  the end of one division and he left and  he kind of left to really discover who  exactly he was after the real vision our  vision kind of made him see everything  that had happened to him so i'm actually  kind of expecting the scarlet witch to  show up in the series now since it's  being rumored and i would not be  surprised in the slightest if vision  returned as well now the end of one  division obviously set up the return for  spectral vision we just didn't know when  he was going to return but this makes a  lot of sense and like i just mentioned 